  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 137 PM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nThrough Tuesday: Local radars were showing isolated showers and \nthunderstorms developing over the northeast portions of the CWA. \nThis activity will increase in coverage this afternoon before \ndissipating shortly after sunset. The convection is expected to \nbring very little relief to the heat and humidity. Heat stress will \nremain the main concern this afternoon and again Tuesday. A Heat \nAdvisory will remain in effect until this evening for the area \ngenerally along and west of Interstate 55 and will be in effect \nagain Tuesday. This is the area where the most oppressive conditions \nwill occur but the remainder of the CWA will see peak heat index \nvalues around 105F this afternoon and again Tuesday. /22/\n\nThrough the weekend: An anomalously strong ridge remains over the\nFour Corners region this, but the Bermuda High is becoming the \ndominant feature in our region as it retrogrades from the Atlantic\nto the Gulf Coast. As it treks westward this week, it will become\na stronger limiting factor for rain chances. High PWAT values \nnear 2 inches will persist in the region through midweek, so \nincreasing heat and humidity will push our daily heat index values\nover 105 degrees each day. Showers and thunderstorms will bring \nspotty relief from the heat. Drier air will wrap from the Gulf and\nsouthwestern US as the ridge becomes more prevalent, and PWAT \nvalues will fall closer to 1.5 inches by on Friday. Model guidance\nis favoring a new surge of tropical moisture by Saturday into \nSunday though, and the stout ridge and deep moisture could result \nin more widespread significant dangerous heat (heat index values \nnear or greater than 110 degrees) by the weekend. Overnight low \ntemps will only fall into the mid or upper 70s later in the week, \nworsening heat stress for vulnerable populations and those without\nair conditioning. And rain chances will creep back in from the \nsouth and east as humidity increases there.\n\nResidents are reminded that heat is particularly dangerous for \nthe elderly, the sick, and those without access to reliable air \nconditioning. Be sure loved ones and neighbors have access to a \ncool place to stay in periods of more intense heat and humidity. \n/NF/22/",
